#/
    Just the order of symbols for references

    Start with `&`                                          A
    For SIMD-representation fat pointers add `:`,           B
    To reference count, add `+`                             C
    Remember, `/` is the symbol of atomicity,               D
    Not to be confused with `\`, the symbol of Objectivity. D
 >  To indicate nullability then add `^`,                   E
 >| To indicate stack-allocation then add `~`               F
  | Unless you have a static reference, then add `'     `   D (apostrophe)
  | Do this as long as you haven't added `+`                C (does this even count it's the same word?)
 >| To indicate immutability then add `.`                   G (full stop)
  | Omit this and it is mutable,                            H
    Then put the type it points to, `T`.                    D

    So to have a SIMD-representation, atomically reference counted, nullable,
    heap-allocated, immutable string, the type is this:
    `&:+/^.[u8]`

    Obeying these rules there are at least 40 different references to `T` (I
    couldn't be fucked to recalculate after adding Objectivity). In total, there
    are at least 45 distinct types of indirection to `T` or to executable data
    (+2 for pointers `*` and `*.`, +1 for function pointers, +2 for closures).

    If a function returns two references, or a vector has two references, that
    type has more than 1600 combinations. If it can return any two indirection
    types, it has more than 2025 combinations.
/#